### Follow one image through the tiers

<figure class="stepper" data-illustrated><span class="stepper-title">One URL, two sizes, one cancelled row</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="viz-grid" data-cols="3"><div class="node" data-el="target" data-art="screen" data-art-role="client"><strong>Feed row</strong><small data-text="targetV">AsyncImage</small></div><div class="node" data-el="memory" data-art="memory" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Memory cache</strong><small data-text="memoryV">decoded bitmaps</small></div><div class="node" data-el="disk" data-art="database" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Disk cache</strong><small data-text="diskV">encoded bytes</small></div></div><div class="viz-grid" data-cols="3"><div class="node" data-el="fetch" data-art="cloud" data-art-role="runtime"><strong>Fetcher</strong><small data-text="fetchV">network source</small></div><div class="node" data-el="decode" data-art="code" data-art-role="runtime"><strong>Decoder</strong><small data-text="decodeV">idle</small></div></div><div class="node is-key" data-el="event" data-art="signal" data-art-role="runtime"><strong>What happens</strong><small data-text="eventV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
  {
    "label": "Memory is checked first",
    "caption": "A feed row asks for an image at 240×240. The memory key combines the URL, the target size, the transformations and the colour space. Nothing matches, so this is a miss.",
    "add": [
      "target",
      "memory",
      "disk",
      "fetch",
      "decode",
